abstract: >
  A structural analysis of the second variation of the moving-sofa area
  functional at Gerver's sofa and at Romik's ambidextrous candidate
  Sigma, on H^2 corner trajectories (modulo translation symmetry). The
  conclusions are largely negative and precise: we identify exactly why
  a second-variation argument does not establish local maximality, and
  reduce the obstruction to a finite, explicitly located quantity.

  VERSION NOTE. This work has been revised repeatedly as the analysis
  sharpened; v0.7.0 supersedes all earlier versions. v0.1.0-v0.4.0
  claimed a strict local maximum on H^2 with an explicit coercivity
  constant; that was withdrawn in v0.5.0 (the constant mixed two inner
  products). v0.6.0 argued the local maximum holds after all via an H^1
  coercivity plus a two-norm theorem; v0.7.0 withdraws that too, because
  the cubic-remainder hypothesis it relied on is false. Readers should
  use v0.7.0.

  WHAT v0.7.0 ESTABLISHES.
  (1) Rank-one degeneracy of the principal symbol. In Lemma 8's form
  C<eta,eta'> + D<eta,eta''>, the matrix D has trace 1 and determinant
  identically 0: it is the rank-one projection onto the binding wall's
  normal. So the one-contact second variation is blind to the tangential
  component of eta' -- and single-wall coercivity is impossible.
  (2) Multi-contact repair. The true symbol sums over the walls binding
  at each theta: D_tot = n_mu (mu mu^T) + n_nu (nu nu^T), with mu, nu
  orthogonal, so its eigenvalues are exactly (n_mu, n_nu). From Romik's
  five phases, min(n_mu, n_nu) = 1 everywhere for Gerver, giving a
  uniform Garding constant lambda_min = 1 (matches the oracle to 3-4
  decimals). A second rank-one degeneracy, C^T C with determinant 0,
  gives ||C||_op = 2 exactly, so the Garding inequality is explicit:
  Q <= -1/2 ||eta'||^2 + 18 ||eta||^2_{L^2}.
  (3) F is piecewise-quadratic. Each contact path is affine in (c,c'),
  so the Green integrand is quadratic in the jet (d^3 L/d eps^3 = 0):
  within a fixed combinatorial cell F is exactly quadratic, and the
  entire third variation is carried by the four MOVING breakpoints
  b_j(c).
  (4) The obstruction, located. Among the moving-breakpoint monomials,
  exactly eta'(b_j)^3 grows fast enough to defeat an H^1 two-norm
  estimate, and its coefficient is measured NONZERO (~1.09 and ~1.89 in
  the two components; controls vanish identically; the two interior
  breakpoints are exact negatives by symmetry). So the improved-Taylor
  hypothesis of Ioffe / Dambrine-Lamboley fails in (H^1, H^2), and no
  such argument closes -- for Gerver as well as Sigma.
  (5) Sigma is doubly obstructed. Its multi-contact symbol is ~4I on the
  middle phase but degenerates at the end caps like lambda_min ~ 4.95
  theta^1.69, so no uniform Garding constant exists there at all.

  CONSEQUENCES. For Gerver, local maximality holds regardless via Baek
  (2024) -- but not via this route. For Sigma no global result exists,
  and local maximality of Sigma (second half of Romik's 2018 Open
  Problem 1) REMAINS OPEN, now with two distinct located reasons. The
  finite-dimensional Hessian uses a floating-point polygon oracle rather
  than interval arithmetic; this affects numerical constants but not the
  structural (symbolic) conclusions.
keywords:
  - moving sofa problem
  - Gerver's sofa
  - ambidextrous sofa
  - Romik
  - local maximality
  - second variation
  - computer-assisted
